  "scope": "Within the fixed Xu--Fu--Qiao--Tao arXiv:2609.04122v1 construction and proof framework specified in problem.md, using the canonical 952 length-54 ternary codewords, the published exact event-volume and dependency construction, and the fixed charges alpha=51/100000 and beta=3/10, C(226) holds: for every integer n>=1 there exists S in {0,1,2}^n such that ED(S[i,j),S[j,k)) >= (k-i)/226 for every 1<=i<j<k<=n+1. This statement does not assert that 226 is the least working denominator.",
